From 1a5fbd01b13e0f69ce9ab0eecdbfad9dbb4fd22a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:30:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/24] clocksource: Add Ingenic X2600 OST driver

The Ingenic X2600 has no system timer that mainline supports: the MIPS
CP0 counter is not implemented in XBurst cores, and the OST differs from
the X1000 SYSOST. It is split in two register blocks: a global 64-bit
counter shared by the cores, and a 32-bit compare timer per core that
interrupts its own core on CPU interrupt line 4.

Use the global counter as clocksource and sched_clock, and each core's
compare timer as that core's clock event device, set up when the core
comes online.

The register layout follows Ingenic's X2600 SDK kernel.
